-- Spawn data recovered from the maintainer's own AzerothCore world DB
-- (acore_world, AC rev 13e8857b515d, mod-playerbots fork) -- GENERATED.
--
-- These 263 units exist in pfQuest but shipped with an EMPTY coords table, so every
-- quest depending on them rendered nothing. pfQuest's own WotLK overlay could not fix
-- them: it only ADDS ids that are missing entirely, so an id present-but-blank was
-- skipped. Questie could fill only part of this set; AzerothCore is the server these
-- players actually play on, so it is preferred wherever it has data.
--
-- Method (same as db/units-wotlk-icecrown335.lua):
--  * World (x,y) -> map percent per zone, fitted EMPIRICALLY from NPCs appearing in both
--    acore_world and pfQuest with a single unambiguous spawn. 67 zones produced a clean
--    model; a zone was REJECTED if its median residual exceeded 1.5%, so nothing is
--    emitted for zones we cannot map reliably.
--  * Each spawn is assigned to a zone by testing which fitted zone's world-space bounding
--    box contains it (smallest containing box wins), converted with that zone's model,
--    and kept only if it lands inside 0..100%.
--  * Near-duplicate points collapsed on a 0.5% grid.
--
-- Cross-checked against Questie for the 60 entries it also knows: 94% identical zone
-- assignment, 92% of nodes within 5%, MEDIAN nearest-node distance 0.01%. Entries where
-- Questie disagreed on the ZONE were dropped rather than shipped (4: [1129, 14848, 21075, 26394]) --
-- AC is preferred, but not against a second source placing the mob somewhere else.
--
-- Instance spawns are deliberately absent: pfQuest cannot resolve dungeon maps on 3.3.5a,
-- so ~1,038 further fillable entries would have rendered nowhere.
--
-- Entries are emitted WHOLE, because patchtable() replaces a key outright rather than
-- merging into it. Two consequences, both enforced when this file is generated:
--  * Every non-coords field of the entry being replaced (lvl, fac, rnk, ...) is copied in
--    verbatim, or replacing the entry would silently DELETE it. A missing lvl/fac shows up
--    as a blank level in tooltips and as a mob that no longer respects faction filtering.
--  * "Empty coords" is decided against the MERGED base (data patched with data-wotlk), not
--    against data alone -- 7 ids looked empty in the vanilla table but already had WotLK
--    spawns, and filling them would have overwritten real data (13956 Winterax Mystic
--    would have dropped from 6 spawns to 1). Those ids are excluded rather than filled:
--    626, 8117, 8118, 12156, 13956, 13957, 13958.
--  * Every coord is the full 4-slot {x, y, zone, respawn} tuple the rest of the database
--    uses. SearchMobID does a bare `respawn > 0`, so a 3-slot tuple throws out of the node
--    builder on every questlog and map update -- that was the v1.0.27 login error.
--
-- Respawn is the creature's own spawntimesecs from acore_world, not a guess: 258 of the
-- 267 units carry one uniform value across every spawn, and the remaining 9 take the most
-- common one. A unit with no AC creature row keeps 0, which pfQuest reads as "Unknown".
local d = pfDB["units"]["data-wotlk"]
